WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:05.650
Our disgusting tale of anomalous nastiness
begins in the humble town of Beckley, West

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:08.380
Virginia, back in the 1990s.

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:13.580
It was 10 AM on a hot day in early August,
as Oscar Duhigg was wending his way through

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.350
the wooded roads and back streets of town.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:21.970
He isn’t the villain of our story, he’s
just a man doing his very unglamorous job:

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:24.730
Cleaning up roadkill for the local government.

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:28.680
Plenty of woodland critters met their ends
against the wheels and bumpers of careless

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:33.170
drivers, and it was thanks to the tireless
work of people like Oscar Duhigg that the

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:37.640
fine roads of rural America aren’t piled
high with carcasses.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:44.830
Of course, Oscar was used to seeing some unpleasant
things on the job, but nothing like this.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:49.201
When he began pulling over to the side of
a lonely street to pick up a dead deer, he

00:00:49.201 --> 00:00:54.050
was shocked to see a sudden flash of stark
white illuminated by his headlights.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:58.360
It was a naked, human woman, crouched over
the deer carcass.

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:02.940
She was sucking at the exposed red flesh on
the deer’s flank, as though feeding off

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:04.040
of it.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.540
Flies circled around her in the hot summer
air.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:12.180
The smell emerging from the deer carcass was
unspeakable, but the woman didn’t even seem

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.490
to care.

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:16.710
She just fed away, with a crazed look in her
eye.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:22.630
And even more disturbing was the fact that
he recognized her: It was Mrs. Faber, a local

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:27.090
eccentric who lived with her husband on a
farm just outside of town.

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:28.790
Or at least, she had.

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:34.600
You see, Oscar Duhigg had never met Mrs. Faber
in person before - he only recognized her

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:37.990
from the missing person fliers posted around
town.

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:42.490
He pulled out his cell phone to call the authorities
when suddenly, Mrs. Faber was startled by

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:45.409
something and fled into the woods.

00:01:45.409 --> 00:01:50.171
This would be the first of many encounters
reported by townsfolk concerning Mrs. Faber

00:01:50.171 --> 00:01:57.460
- or more specifically, the anomalous species
that once was Mrs. Faber, and is now designated

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:00.150
SCP-726.

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:04.869
Mrs. Faber practically became a local cryptid,
similar to that of sasquatch or the Loch Ness

00:02:04.869 --> 00:02:09.700
Monster with sightings of her in the woods
and around town frequently being reported

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:11.060
by the locals.

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:15.000
Of course, Mr. Faber was beside himself about
this whole situation.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.910
What was happening to his beloved wife?

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:22.760
People assumed a psychotic break or some kind
of sudden onset of acute dementia.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:27.770
She had to be apprehended and brought in for
her own good before she caused harm to herself

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:29.380
or others.

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:33.730
And on August 16th, she was finally found
and captured.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:38.160
Mrs. Faber was found in the dumpster of a
local diner with a large dog.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:41.200
After being subdued, she was sent to a nearby
hospital.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:45.420
Her condition had seemingly advanced to the
point where she was no longer even capable

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:46.599
of speech.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:51.500
However, if it had ended there, the SCP Foundation
wouldn’t have been called in.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:56.130
It would have just been a sad local story
of a woman who became very unwell.

00:02:56.130 --> 00:03:01.680
But that was only the beginning to the true
strangeness behind SCP-726.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:06.890
Random livestock, like cows and pigs, were
found across the town, behaving incredibly

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:11.650
bizarre - exhibiting actions and traits uncommon
of their respective species.

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:16.680
And the most shocking of all was that the
sightings of Mrs. Faber around town still

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:21.020
didn’t stop, despite her being actively
held by a local hospital.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:26.380
Naturally, that’s when the SCP Foundation
decided to take control of the situation.

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:30.970
They dispatched field agents to properly investigate
and figure out what was going on in Beckley,

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:32.080
West Virginia.

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:35.890
That’s when they discovered a peculiar commonality:
Maggots.

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:41.930
You see, the behavior exhibited by the strange
animals and by Mrs. Faber was not consistent

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:46.690
with their own species, but they were incredibly
consistent with the behaviors of the common

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:52.620
botfly - a particularly unpleasant form of
fly that sometimes lays its eggs in the bodies

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.730
of still-living animals.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:04:00.200
The anomalously affected entities exhibited
insectoid movements, an affinity for rotting

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:05.300
meat, and even strange shifting of the back
muscles, suggesting the gesture of flapping

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:07.459
wings that weren’t there.

00:04:07.459 --> 00:04:09.230
But what was going on here?

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:13.300
Was this mind control, or something more insidious?

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:18.101
As it turned out, the key to unlocking this
mystery was in the dumpster that Mrs. Faber

00:04:18.101 --> 00:04:19.329
was found in.

00:04:19.329 --> 00:04:24.820
An entire pig was found inside the dumpster,
exhibiting the same strange behaviors as the

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:26.280
other anomalous animals.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:31.630
But not long before it was transformed into
a pig, it was simply a half-eaten hot dog

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:34.080
thrown to waste in the garbage.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:42.040
This miraculous transformation came courtesy
of SCP-726, now also known as the Reconstructive

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:43.040
Maggots.

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:47.730
Much like regular maggots, these creatures
are attracted to decaying flesh and will multiply

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:50.919
and consume dead bodies or rotten food rapidly.

00:04:50.919 --> 00:04:54.770
However, the truly strange thing is what happens
afterward.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:05:00.360
The maggots will expel purified waste matter,
which then reconstitutes back into a kind

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:05.030
of living, exact clone of the entity it once
was.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:07.490
Well, “exact” in a physical sense.

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:12.139
In a psychological sense, these clones are
exactly like a mature botfly.

00:05:12.139 --> 00:05:16.729
The maggots that reconstitute these bodies
die off almost immediately, but whenever two

00:05:16.729 --> 00:05:22.760
of these clones mate - with reproductive behavior
often being inspired by the presence of carcasses

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:30.199
or spoilt meat - they produce more eggs, which
in turn release SCP-726 maggots and begin

00:05:30.199 --> 00:05:33.340
the cycle all over again.

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:38.781
And fascinatingly, these maggots can reconstitute
an entire clone from even a portion of the

00:05:38.781 --> 00:05:40.450
original creature.

00:05:40.450 --> 00:05:46.090
Which begs the question: Why were there seemingly
multiple Mrs. Fabers sighted in and around

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:48.720
the town of Beckley, West Virginia?

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:54.020
Upon further investigation into Mrs. Faber
and her husband, a terrible secret came to

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:58.860
light: Mr. Faber had murdered his wife in
a fit of rage and cut up her body, before

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:02.199
burying the pieces around the grounds of his
home.

00:06:02.199 --> 00:06:09.169
Unbeknownst to him, an infestation of SCP-726
maggots across the property ate each piece

00:06:09.169 --> 00:06:14.790
and reconstituted them into individual, fly-brained
clones of the original.

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:18.900
Mr. Faber was later arrested for the murder,
and multiple people in the town of Beckley

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:23.960
were given amnestic treatment to forget the
strange and frightening things they’d seen.

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:29.700
But for the Foundation, the strange and frightening
things were only just beginning.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:34.800
An unnamed doctor with the SCP Foundation
decided to conduct a series of utterly repulsive

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:41.430
experiments on SCP-726, opening the log with
the fateful words, “I've decided to begin

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:44.479
by testing the limits of repeated replication.

00:06:44.479 --> 00:06:48.800
A single SCP-726 egg will be introduced per
sample.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:53.580
Due to their rapid multiplication, maggot
volume does not affect their speed of operation,

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:56.610
only the size of the organism to be reconstructed.”

00:06:56.610 --> 00:07:02.110
The first subject was a recently deceased
Norwegian rat, cut in half lengthwise.

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:07.569
When the SCP-726 eggs were introduced, the
two halves were rapidly constituted into a

00:07:07.569 --> 00:07:11.289
pair of living rats with mirrored fur patterns.

00:07:11.289 --> 00:07:17.419
Both of these rats were then ground into a
fine paste, and mixed, wondering if SCP-726

00:07:17.419 --> 00:07:19.640
would create a hybrid.

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:25.919
They did not, instead separating the mix into
two piles and once again creating two rats,

00:07:25.919 --> 00:07:31.860
nearly identical to the ones before - except
for one of them now having a red right eye.

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:36.900
The rat without the red right eye was processed
into a fine paste - get used to hearing that

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:41.620
phrase - before the introduction of more SCP-726
samples.

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:46.759
It reproduced a close approximation of the
rat it once was, aside from a slight limp

00:07:46.759 --> 00:07:48.870
and blindness in both eyes.

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:54.020
The heart was then taken from this rat, and
upon the introduction of SCP-726 into the

00:07:54.020 --> 00:07:57.949
heart, it was reconstituted without eyes or
any pigmentation.

00:07:57.949 --> 00:08:02.540
A note also mentions that the creature squeaked
incessantly.

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:08.680
The heart from this rat was then taken and
cut in half before SCP-726 was introduced.

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:13.639
The result was a pair of even more severely
messed-up, eyeless rats.

00:08:13.639 --> 00:08:18.300
One could only walk in tight circles, and
the other immediately attacked the first rat.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:23.110
The doctor noted that both physiology and
insect behavior seems to degrade with repeated

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:25.740
reconstitutions of the same genetic material.

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:29.770
Next, a scrap of flesh was taken from the
hairless rat.

00:08:29.770 --> 00:08:35.509
The creature that reconstituted from this
was hairless, eyeless, and limbless, and didn’t

00:08:35.509 --> 00:08:37.360
successfully survive for long.

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:40.339
A liver was found inside its braincase.

00:08:40.339 --> 00:08:45.600
But because this particular researcher hadn’t
spit in the face of god enough for one day,

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:47.489
the tests continued.

00:08:47.489 --> 00:08:53.629
The liver from the brainless rat was given
a dose of SCP-726, and the result was an eyeless,

00:08:53.629 --> 00:08:58.930
legless, limbless creature with a long, wormlike
midsection, which quickly began to devour

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:02.209
its own posterior before dying of blood loss.

00:09:02.209 --> 00:09:06.489
This dead rat was then put through three more
iterations of testing.

00:09:06.489 --> 00:09:11.339
It first became a large, formless mass of
tissue, and then a long, slug-like creature

00:09:11.339 --> 00:09:13.970
that takes in nutrients through its skin.

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:19.699
After this, no more changes were recorded,
as it had presumably reached peak performance.

00:09:19.699 --> 00:09:25.689
The scientist decided to keep this creature
for long-term observation, naming it “Brundle”,

00:09:25.689 --> 00:09:29.510
after the scientist in David Cronenberg’s
remake of “The Fly.”

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:34.699
At this point, the doctor began to conduct
tests that, mercifully, did not involve any

00:09:34.699 --> 00:09:36.009
more rats.

00:09:36.009 --> 00:09:39.220
Instead, the Foundation moved on to humans.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:44.930
Dried flesh from a body that’s over 2000
years old was given to SCP-726, leading to

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:50.269
a full reconstitution of a middle-aged man
with the mind of a fly - opening doors to

00:09:50.269 --> 00:09:55.439
potential practical forensic applications
of SCP-726.

00:09:55.439 --> 00:10:00.279
Humans seem to experience a similar degree
of form degradation after multiple reconstitutions

00:10:00.279 --> 00:10:06.540
from the same genetic material, but due to
humans being larger and more complex organisms,

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:11.699
the changes are often less pronounced - like
changes in eye color or fingerprints.

00:10:11.699 --> 00:10:18.459
While the forensic use of SCP-726 is an open
door, clones produced by SCP-726 are worthless

00:10:18.459 --> 00:10:21.429
for both medical and food purposes.

00:10:21.429 --> 00:10:26.589
During one experiment, SCP-726 was used to
replace a missing chunk of a wounded D-Class’

00:10:26.589 --> 00:10:28.019
leg.

00:10:28.019 --> 00:10:33.299
This appeared to be successful at first, until
the D-Class later experienced a rapid mental

00:10:33.299 --> 00:10:39.309
devolution into a fly-like state, just like
the other victims of SCP-726.

00:10:39.309 --> 00:10:43.209
The D-Class was terminated and the test was
recorded as a failure.

00:10:43.209 --> 00:10:48.290
It’s believed that a similar thing would
happen if organ transplants were taken out

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:52.470
of SCP-726 clones and given to non-anomalous
donors.

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:58.470
SCP-726 was used to clone several livestock
animals, such as cows and pigs.

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:03.519
Food items like steaks were rendered from
these animals, cooked, and given to D-Classes.

00:11:03.519 --> 00:11:08.399
Much like the transplants, this led to a similar
state of devolution for those who ate the

00:11:08.399 --> 00:11:10.040
infected meat.

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:15.059
Even when the meat was thoroughly disinfected
and processed, the anomalous effects remained.

00:11:15.059 --> 00:11:20.850
So no, SCP-726 won’t be ending world hunger
any time soon.

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:25.089
Though if it gave us all the minds of flies
through tainted meat, it may at least end

00:11:25.089 --> 00:11:30.129
all global warfare, seeing as flies don’t
have the mental capacity to create or wield

00:11:30.129 --> 00:11:31.129
weapons.

00:11:31.129 --> 00:11:35.709
At this point, it seemed that the researcher
was just curious, and felt like trying some

00:11:35.709 --> 00:11:38.709
other random experiments, just for the heck
of it.

00:11:38.709 --> 00:11:44.670
Like getting SCP-726 to reconstitute a non-anomalous
botfly, leading to the clone simply being

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:48.959
an unusually large botfly, which died shortly
thereafter.

00:11:48.959 --> 00:11:53.519
Or testing a burger patty from a local independent
drive-through restaurant, that reconstituted

00:11:53.519 --> 00:11:56.799
into two different cows and one large rat.

00:11:56.799 --> 00:11:57.799
Yummy!

00:11:57.799 --> 00:12:03.499
But the most horrifying result of all came
when they tested SCP-726 on what was supposedly

00:12:03.499 --> 00:12:08.170
a vegan burger made entirely out of artificial
meat and plant matter.

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:13.630
The resulting creatures were so unimaginably
horrifying, they literally cannot be described.

00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:18.429
Even hardened SCP Foundation researchers were
driven to scream and vomit at the mere sight

00:12:18.429 --> 00:12:19.429
of them.

00:12:19.429 --> 00:12:24.999
One of these creatures was killed and ground
into a fine paste before SCP-726 was introduced

00:12:24.999 --> 00:12:25.999
again.

00:12:25.999 --> 00:12:31.899
Somehow, this resulted in something even worse,
a truly horrifying, unkillable entity on par

00:12:31.899 --> 00:12:34.739
with SCP-682.

00:12:34.739 --> 00:12:37.970
Even when they liquefied the beast, it kept
attacking.

00:12:37.970 --> 00:12:41.829
They could only stop it by freezing it and
keeping it on ice.

00:12:41.829 --> 00:12:45.970
Testing into SCP-726 was suspended shortly
afterward.

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:50.290
Aaahhh - maggots, botflies and rat paste - how
lovely.

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:55.480
If you were eating during any of this, well,
you only have yourself to blame.

00:12:55.480 --> 00:13:02.799
Now go check out “SCP-2852 Sadistic Madman
Party Crasher | Cousin Johnny” and “SCP-5049

00:13:02.799 --> 00:13:08.049
- The Skin Salesman - Demon Dan's Discount
Homunculus Depot” for terrifying tales of

00:13:08.049 --> 00:13:08.949
anomalous body horror!

